  "notes": "{賛成|さんせい} expresses being in favor of something — an opinion, proposal, or plan.\n\nGRAMMAR:\nTakes the particle に to mark what you agree with: その{案|あん}に{賛成|さんせい}する (to agree with that proposal).\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- {賛成|さんせい}する: to agree, to approve\n- 〜に{賛成|さんせい}だ: to be in agreement with ~\n- {賛成|さんせい}{多数|たすう}: majority in favor\n- {賛成|さんせい}{派|は}: supporters, pro-faction\n- {賛成|さんせい}{意見|いけん}: opinion in favor\n\nIN VOTING:\n- {賛成|さんせい}! (Aye!) vs. {反対|はんたい}! (Nay!)\n- {賛成|さんせい}{多数|たすう}で{可決|かけつ}: passed by majority vote\n\nANTONYM:\n- {反対|はんたい}: opposition, disagreement (direct opposite)",
